      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "chat-provenance-class"
        },
        "markdown": "# Chat Provenance\n\nEach node represents exactly **one conversation**. A graph may accumulate many Chat provenance nodes as it is created, revised, reviewed, and explained.\n\nThe durable record is the Twilite node. The discussion URL is a source doorway, not the node identity. Every node should keep a local summary so it remains useful when a link is private, revoked, deleted, or unavailable.\n\nRelationship meaning belongs on the graph edge: `created`, `revised`, `reviewed`, `explained`, or `inspired`.\n\nThis class does **not** expose commit history or reconstruct prior graph states."
      }
    },
